-name beamchain@127.0.0.1

## No cookie is set here: one committed in this file would be the same on every
## install, and anyone holding it who can reach the distribution port can
## run arbitrary code in the node. Without one, the runtime reads
## $HOME/.erlang.cookie and, if it is absent, generates a random cookie
## there on first boot (mode 0400), so each install has its own. Set
## RELX_COOKIE to supply one explicitly.

## Distribution listens on loopback only (-name alone binds every interface)
-kernel inet_dist_use_interface {127,0,0,1}

## An EPMD started by this VM listens on loopback only
-env ERL_EPMD_ADDRESS 127.0.0.1

## Process limit — 1M processes for concurrent peer/block handling
+P 1048576

## Enable kernel polling for better I/O scalability
+K true

## Async thread pool for NIF/driver I/O (RocksDB, secp256k1)
+A 64

## Reduce fullsweep GC frequency for long-lived processes
-env ERL_FULLSWEEP_AFTER 10

## Increase atom table for dynamic peer/config atoms
+t 1048576
